+// SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-2.0
+/*
+ * Shortcut for established IPv4 and IPv6 flows on the Octeon receive path.
+ *
+ * The CN50xx has no separate NAT engine. EdgeOS got its speed by rewriting
+ * a buffer the packet hardware already held and handing it back to the
+ * output unit. This does the same kind of thing with the information Linux
+ * already has: when flow offload is on, nftables calls into the driver and we
+ * keep a copy of each TCP/UDP flow. The receive loop looks that copy up
+ * before netif_receive_skb. A hit rewrites the headers and transmits with
+ * the driver's normal PKO send. Anything else takes the existing path.
+ *
+ * PPPoE session data is popped on the way in and pushed on the way out.
+ * One 802.1Q tag is the same, and it sits outside the session header when
+ * both are present. The session id and the VLAN id have to match the flow.
+ * IPv4 inside the session is PPP protocol 0x0021. IPv6 is 0x0057. Routed
+ * IPv6 only decrements the hop limit. The same SNAT and DNAT flags as IPv4
+ * rewrite the addresses. Discovery, LCP, a second VLAN tag, fragments, IP
+ * options, IPv6 extension headers, a UDP checksum of zero, FIN/RST, a hop
+ * limit or TTL of 1, and a bridge with a non-Octeon port up or two live
+ * Octeon ports stay on the normal path. The receive path turns on when a
+ * hardware flowtable binds one of these ports, and turns off when the last
+ * port unbinds.
+ *
+ * The word2 bits read below are the CN50xx layout. That is the UniFi
+ * Security Gateway and the EdgeRouter Lite. CN68xx and the Octeon III
+ * boards that share this driver (EdgeRouter 4 and 6P) are left on the
+ * normal path: a wrong read could rewrite a packet that should have
+ * stayed there.
+ *
+ * The EdgeRouter 12 (Cavium CN7130, Octeon III) is added here. CN71xx
+ * reads the same word2.s fields as CN50xx and does not carry the PKND
+ * feature, so the same parse applies. The ip_offset cross-check in the
+ * receive path is the safety net for a layout surprise: a mismatch
+ * shows up as a permanent miss, not as a corrupted packet.
+ */
+
